# Advanced settings for DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash on four CMP 170HX cards.
#
# You almost certainly don't need anything here: the common settings are in
# .env.example. ./start.sh reads only .env, so to use a setting from this
# file, copy its line into your .env (not into this file) and uncomment it.
# Every line shows the default the scripts or the release's launch use when it
# is unset, so a later release's new defaults reach you on ./start.sh update
# without editing .env. Delete or re-comment a line to go back to the default.
# The paths (/path/to/...) and HF_TOKEN lines are placeholders, not defaults;
# the note above each says what the default is.
#
# Format: KEY=value, one per line, notes on their own lines starting with #.
# An unquoted value ends at the first " #" (whitespace then #), and a trailing
# "  (...)" (two or more spaces, then a note in parentheses) is dropped too, so
# a note left on the line does not end up in the value. A # or ( that is part
# of the value (a#b, f(x)) is kept. Quote the value, "..." or '...', to keep
# everything between the quotes exactly as written.
# A prefix env assignment overrides .env for every key, including an
# explicit empty (KEY= ./start.sh):   MAX_SEQS=4 ./start.sh restart
#
# The engine switches are documented, with their use for troubleshooting, in
# docs/engine-switches.md. The release's launch sets each of them; a line here
# overrides it.

# === weights ============================================================
# Weights to download, pinned to the Hub revisions this release was validated
# with (./start.sh and Docker Compose fetch exactly these). The hybrid built
# from them must match the validated bytes, so other revisions stop the start.
# EXPORT_REPO=LibertAIDAI/DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash-1017-EXL3-2.9bpw
# EXPORT_REVISION=c178a01284fc5c0e859d8668cffaac81ca8f4042
# OFFICIAL_REPO=deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash-1017
# OFFICIAL_REVISION=1bae0e1088993b9b82de08f59de5be5a34e42170
# Unauthenticated Hub downloads are rate limited; a token is faster.
# HF_TOKEN=hf_xxx
# 1 checks the downloads again with the Hub even when they are complete.
# REFRESH_WEIGHTS=0

# === serving limits =====================================================
# Concurrent sequences.
# MAX_SEQS=8
# Scheduler token budget per step (the prefill chunk).
# MAX_BATCHED=2048
# Appended to the vllm serve command line, split at whitespace, e.g. a shorter
# context: --max-model-len 131072
# EXTRA_ARGS=
# Seconds ./start.sh waits for /health. Weight load, the Engram tables and
# CUDA-graph capture are slow.
# READY_TIMEOUT=3600
# After health: exactly two requests check OK and drafting. 0 disables.
# BOOT_CHECK=1
# Seconds ./start.sh stop waits for a clean shutdown.
# STOP_TIMEOUT=120

# === container ==========================================================
# The engine image, by digest (default: this release's, pinned in start.sh).
# IMAGE=ghcr.io/morrowmake/vllm-cmp170hx@sha256:f67d9be47ffbd4a8b84c77fe76bdb3f842187d9b2786fff573e390ae5361bfb0
# Name of the container ./start.sh runs. Only a container this checkout
# started (recorded in logs/container.id) is ever stopped.
# CONTAINER_NAME=dsv41-flash
# Shared memory for the container (the host-memory all-reduce and NCCL use it).
# SHM_SIZE=16g
# The container's memory limit, swap included, so the server never swaps
# (swapped-out Engram tables cost ~8 % of prefill speed). Default: the host's
# memory (./start.sh), or 1024g, above any host's (Docker Compose).
# MEM_LIMIT=256g
# Kernel compile caches, kept between starts. Default: cache/ in this repo.
# CACHE_DIR=/path/to/cache

# === preflight ==========================================================
# The preflight stops, before any download, if fewer than MIN_GPUS cards are
# visible or a card reports less than MIN_GPU_MIB (60 GiB). NEED_DISK_GB is in
# GiB (the checkpoints take ~672 GiB). NEED_RAM_GIB is the host memory the
# Engram tables in RAM need: below it VLLM_ENGRAM_PLACEMENT=auto reads them
# from the SSD, and an explicit ram stops before the start.
# MIN_GPUS=4
# MIN_GPU_MIB=61440
# NEED_DISK_GB=680
# NEED_RAM_GIB=212

# === Engram tables ======================================================
# auto takes ram when NEED_RAM_GIB is available, else ssd. ssd reads the
# tables from the checkpoint files instead of host RAM, through a row cache in
# host RAM per card. Under ssd these are chosen unless set: the cache size in
# GiB per card ((available - 29) / 4, 1 to 48), filling it at start (1 for a
# cache of 12 GiB or more; it reads ~49 GB per card), and direct reads of the
# misses (0 on a file system that refuses them).
# VLLM_ENGRAM_PLACEMENT=auto
# VLLM_ENGRAM_ROW_CACHE_GIB=
# VLLM_ENGRAM_ROW_CACHE_PRELOAD=
# VLLM_ENGRAM_DIRECT_READ=

# === peer access ========================================================
# P2P=auto in .env.example verifies content before enabling it.
# A topology OK result alone cannot prove that peer data reaches its owner.
# Disable the custom all-reduce after a pass (NCCL P2P remains enabled):
# VLLM_CUSTOM_ALLREDUCE_PCIE_P2P=0
# Optional persistent check cache; defaults to $HOME/.cache/recipe-p2p.
# P2P_CHECK_CACHE=/path/to/p2p-cache
# Use runtime compilation instead of the matching image probe:
# P2P_PREBUILT=0

# === engine switches ====================================================
# Each is set by the release's launch; copy a line into .env with 0 to switch
# that feature off, then restart. See docs/engine-switches.md for what each
# does and which ones need another.
# VLLM_DEEPSEEK_V41_ATTN_PIPELINE=1
# VLLM_DEEPSEEK_V41_FUSED_ROUTE=1
# VLLM_DEEPSEEK_V41_GATE_GEMV=1
# VLLM_DEEPSEEK_V41_ROUTER_MMA=1
# VLLM_EXL3_MOE_V2=1
# VLLM_DEEPSEEK_V41_MOE_PREFILL_TC=1
# VLLM_DEEPSEEK_V41_PREFILL_CE_ALLREDUCE=1
# VLLM_DEEPSEEK_V41_PREFILL_SPLIT_REDUCE=1
# VLLM_HOST_ALLREDUCE=1

# Use the image's compiled-kernel cache when it carries one (this release's
# carries none; 0 disables).
# VLLM_IMAGE_CACHE_SEED=0
